## Repair assessment

`runtimeModelPolicy.ts:758–775` classifies native errors using the imported ConvexError instance/prototype, exact own data-value descriptor, plain data prototype, own field descriptors, version1, retryable=false, outcome not_dispatched/uncertain and an explicit10-code allowlist. It does not infer control authority from error messages. No data/code/version/retryable/outcome/message/cause getters execute. Unknown structured codes, malformed envelopes, plain errors/objects/primitives, missing/inherited/accessor data, nonnative prototypes and classifier-inspection failures return false from the classifier. The outer catch at `:788–790` then throws the original value; no replacement error or cause loss occurs. The exact native envelope provenance is established by runtimeAuth deny/ambiguity, runtimeMemoryRepository memoryError and ledger fail/synchronous PURE domainControl. The latter remains narrowly scoped to synchronous domain calls; a database error whose message resembles POLICY_DENIED never crosses that message adapter.

The first healthy known capture decides delivery eligibility at `:825` **before** accounting/marker writes. An unexpected eligibility query fault therefore aborts with all reserve/slot/charge/marker/account/operation rows unchanged; the same exact receipt after recovery accounts full40 once, releases the slot once and yields pending. Attachment at `:844` now distinguishes recognized eligibility loss from read failure. Unexpected read failure propagates without closing; exact recovery succeeds once. Genuine native control denial/direct current expiry still closes pending permanently, with no monetary change. The existing legacy permittedResult helper and all accepted accounting/refinement/settlement logic are unchanged by C2.

